# Generic Blargg "screen output" test harness.
#
# Several Blargg test ROMs (notably halt_bug, interrupt_time) report
# pass / fail only by drawing ASCII to the LCD via shell.inc's screen
# backend — no serial output.  shell.inc stores ASCII codes directly
# into the BG tile map (the font glyph for each ASCII char is loaded
# into the matching VRAM tile slot at boot), so reading $9800/$9C00
# back as bytes yields the on-screen text verbatim.  `run-until
# bg-text-match` does the substring search at every VBlank edge.
#
# Works for the serial-emitting ROMs too (cpu_instrs, instr_timing,
# mem_timing, mem_timing-2) since they paint the same text to screen
# in parallel — keeps the whole Blargg suite on one harness.
#
# 500M T-cycles ≈ 119 seconds of emulated GB time.  CTest's wall-clock
# timeout (set per-test in test/CMakeLists.txt) caps the real-time
# budget on top of this.
run-until bg-text-match "Passed" max-cycles 500000000
dump bg-text
exit
